  <header>
    <span class="avatar">KK</span>
    <div>
      <h1 id="title">Planning board</h1>
      <div class="sub" id="meta"></div>
    </div>
    <select id="project-picker" hidden></select>
    <button class="pill" id="config-btn" aria-haspopup="dialog">⚙ Configure</button>
  </header>
  <dialog id="config-panel">
    <div class="cfg-head">
      <h2>Configuration</h2>
      <button class="cfg-close" id="config-close">Close</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cfg-layout">
      <nav class="cfg-nav" id="cfg-nav">
        <button class="cfg-nav-item" data-pane="appearance" aria-current="true">Appearance</button>
        <button class="cfg-nav-item" data-pane="capacity">Capacity</button>
        <button class="cfg-nav-item" data-pane="roster">Roster</button>
        <button class="cfg-nav-item" data-pane="overrides">Calendar overrides</button>
        <button class="cfg-nav-item" data-pane="integrations">Integrations</button>
      </nav>
      <div class="cfg-panes">
        <div class="cfg-pane" data-pane="appearance">
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Theme</h3>
            <div class="cfg-row" id="flavor-picker"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Accent</h3>
            <div class="cfg-row" id="accent-picker"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cfg-pane" data-pane="capacity" hidden>
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Capacity</h3>
            <div class="cfg-fields">
              <label>Workdays per cycle <input type="number" id="cfg-workdays" min="1" max="7" /></label>
              <label>On-call penalty <input type="number" id="cfg-oncall-penalty" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" /></label>
              <label>Default velocity <input type="number" id="cfg-default-velocity" min="0" /></label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cfg-pane" data-pane="roster" hidden>
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Roster</h3>
            <div id="cfg-roster" class="cfg-roster"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cfg-pane" data-pane="overrides" hidden>
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Calendar overrides</h3>
            <p class="cfg-hint">
              Setting on-call or out-days here makes it hand-typed: a refresh leaves it alone. Clearing a
              value back to blank removes that protection instead of confirming "no" — a later refresh
              can still fill it back in. Check "locked" to also freeze a value a refresh already wrote.
            </p>
            <div id="cfg-overrides" class="cfg-overrides"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cfg-pane" data-pane="integrations" hidden>
          <div class="cfg-section">
            <h3>Integrations</h3>
            <p class="cfg-hint">Refreshes on-call, out-days, and velocity (Incident.io, Google Calendar,
              cycle history) and re-fetches issues and roster from Linear — the same as running
              <code>deno task capacity</code> and <code>deno task issues</code>.</p>
            <button class="pill" id="cfg-refresh">Refresh all</button>
            <pre id="cfg-refresh-log" class="cfg-refresh-log" hidden></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cfg-actions">
      <span id="cfg-status" class="cfg-status"></span>
      <button class="pill" id="cfg-save">Save</button>
    </div>
  </dialog>
  <div id="freshness" class="freshness" role="status" hidden></div>
  <div class="bar-controls">
    <input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search id / title / description…" />
    <button class="chip" id="view" aria-pressed="false">Timeline</button>
    <button class="chip" id="expand" aria-pressed="false">Expand</button>
    <button class="chip" id="orient" aria-pressed="false">Rows: people</button>
    <span class="sync-box">
      <span id="sync" class="sync-text"></span>
      <button class="chip" id="refresh">Refresh</button>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="bar-filters">
    <span class="fgroup">
      <span class="flabel">Status</span>
      <span class="chips" id="status-chips"></span>
      <span class="fbulk"><button class="chip mini" id="status-all" title="Show every status">All</button><button class="chip mini" id="status-none" title="Hide every status">None</button></span>
    </span>
    <span class="fgroup">
      <span class="flabel">Bucket</span>
      <span class="chips" id="bucket-chips"></span>
      <span class="fbulk"><button class="chip mini" id="bucket-all" title="Show every column">All</button><button class="chip mini" id="bucket-none" title="Hide every column">None</button></span>
    </span>
    <span class="fgroup"><span class="flabel">Flags</span><span class="chips" id="flag-chips"></span></span>
    <span class="fhint">tip: double-click a chip to show only it</span>
  </div>
  <div class="summary" id="summary"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <table id="grid" aria-label="Planning board: issues by assignee and cycle or milestone"></table>
    <div id="timeline" hidden></div>
  </div>
  <div id="tip"></div>
  <details class="legend">
    <summary>How to read this board</summary>
    <div class="legend-body">
      <p>
        Placement: an issue in an active cycle shows in that cycle's column, otherwise its milestone,
        otherwise Backlog. Capacity heat is a forecast against each person's effective capacity: a base
        velocity (20 points per cycle by default) cut down by on-call weeks and days out of office, with
        milestone columns scaled by the weeks in their window. A cell shows 📟 on-call, 🧳 time off, and
        an "over" badge when committed points exceed that capacity. Hover any ticket for its full title,
        assignee, milestone, relations, and the reason for a flag.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>⚠ slop</b> scans the description for AI tells: dashes, semicolons, checklists, length, and
          stock phrases. A false positive can be marked "not slop" from the hover card; it stays cleared
          until the ticket text changes.</li>
        <li><b>⛔ ordering risk</b> means a blocker finishes after the issue it blocks.</li>
        <li><b>◑ missing</b> marks an absent estimate, assignee, or milestone, but only for issues already
          committed to a cycle.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Filters: double-click a Status or Bucket chip to show only that one (double-click again to
        restore). "Rows: people / buckets" flips the grid so buckets run down the side when heavy
        filtering leaves few columns. The board re-fetches every five minutes and on Refresh without
        touching your filters or scroll position.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keyboard: Tab into the grid, then use the arrow keys to move between tickets. Enter or Space
        opens the focused ticket in Linear, "s" marks it not-slop (or re-flags it) when it carries a
        slop warning, and Escape dismisses the card.
      </p>
      <p>
        "Timeline" flips to a dependency-ordered view: issues are grouped into waves by how deep they sit
        in the blocking graph (wave 1 has no blockers, each later wave depends only on earlier ones). Each
        card shows where it is scheduled, so a card scheduled before its blocker stands out as an ordering
        risk. Issues with no blocking relations are left out of this view.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
